<p>This script stages and deduplicates policy transaction data from XML-flattened source tables, then merges the processed records into a downstream mart table. It handles data type casting, business logic for indicator fields, and ensures only the latest record per policy and transaction date is loaded.</p>

<h3>High-Level Flow</h3>
<p>The script executes in sequence: 1) Run the dependent notebook <code>staging_transformations_logic</code> to create temporary source views. 2) Query and join the source views (<code>vw_policy_xml_raw</code> and <code>vw_account_xml_raw</code>), applying transformations and casting. 3) Deduplicate records using a window function partitioned by <code>policy_number</code> and <code>transaction_effective_date</code>, keeping the most recent by <code>load_ts</code>. 4) Create a temporary view <code>vw_policy_transaction_stage</code>. 5) Execute a SQL MERGE statement to upsert data into the target table <code>mart.policy_transaction</code>.</p>

