<p>Stage and deduplicate policy transaction data from XML-flattened source tables, then merge into a downstream mart table. The script transforms raw policy and account data, ensures uniqueness per policy and transaction date, and performs an upsert into the target.</p>

<h3>High-Level Flow</h3>
<p>1. Execute dependent notebook <code>staging_transformations_logic</code> to create temporary views <code>vw_policy_xml_raw</code> and <code>vw_account_xml_raw</code>.<br>2. Query and join these views to build a staging DataFrame (<code>stg_df</code>) with business logic and casting.<br>3. Apply a window function to deduplicate records, keeping the latest load per <code>policy_number</code> and <code>transaction_effective_date</code>.<br>4. Create a temporary view <code>vw_policy_transaction_stage</code> from the deduplicated DataFrame.<br>5. Execute a SQL MERGE statement to insert or update records in the target table <code>mart.policy_transaction</code>.</p>

